	(text "Connector: J50 USB-C (Wuerth 632723300011, 24-pin), U50 LVDS fan-out, U51/U52 ESD, J51 scope header (revision 4, decision 14)."
		(exclude_from_sim yes)
		(at 38.1 12.7 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.5 2.5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "f5ff80a6-089e-4b34-8785-5811ccb0b1cd")
	)
	(text "Design intent (Rev A revision 4, 2026-10-09, decision 14; PROPOSED unless labelled; nothing here is simulated or measured)\nONE CONNECTOR: J50 carries 5 V (VBUS pins A4/A9/B4/B9 tied, hierarchical output VBUS to the Power eFuse and the Controller), USB 2.0 D+/D- (A6/B6 tied\n  = USB_DP, A7/B7 tied = USB_DM), the 50 Mbps LVDS pair on both SuperSpeed TX pairs through the fan-out U50 (1Y/1Z -> B2/B3, 2Y/2Z -> A2/A3, so the pairs do not cross between U50 and the clamps), CAN on\n  both RX pairs (CAN_H = B11 and A11, CAN_L = B10 and A10) and the SBU pair tied as AUX (A8/B8 -> AUX_CAB -> R186 1k -> AUX). Plug orientation does\n  not matter: N to SSTXp and P to SSTXn on BOTH pairs (USB Type-C R2.5 Table 3-10 p.83; polarity flipped at J50 on 2026-10-09 for layout, consistent on both\n  pairs, so the cable carries the fan-out output inverted; with LVDS_P low for a logic one this makes SSTXp high for a one).\nRd/CC: R181 and R184 5.1 k 1 % on CC1 and CC2 (Type-C R2.0 Table 4-25 p.236). Taps 100k/100k with 100 nF give CC1_SENSE and CC2_SENSE for the ESP32\n  ADC; 100k/100k keeps the pin below 3.3 V even with 5.5 V VCONN on the unused CC (TC R2.5 p.155). The 200 k tap lowers Rd by about 2.5 %: fold into\n  firmware thresholds.\nU50 SN65LVDS104PW (LVDS104 SLLS396G p.3-5, p.16 Fig. 25): no on-chip termination, so R180 100 ohm 0.1 % across A/B is FITTED; enables active high\n  (section 9.4 Table 2), EN1-EN3 to 3V3, EN4 to GND (output 4 disabled, 4Y/4Z no_connect), output 3 feeds J51 with R177 100 ohm DNP across it\n  (UNRESOLVED whether an unloaded output 3 is acceptable). 23 mA typ, 35 mA max (p.5). VOD 250/350/450 mV (TLV3605 p.7) against the 100 mV buffer\n  threshold: 150 mV margin at minimum VOD (arithmetic). Fail-safe: static high with no TLV3605 power (p.15-16). Do NOT add a second 100 ohm at the\n  FPGA without DIFFRESISTOR consideration: the ECP5 input is terminated on-die (DIFFRESISTOR 100, docs/research/ulx3s-lvds-input.md); each of the two\n  paths sees one load.\nESD: U51 (pin 14 CC1 A5, 13 spare, 12/11 SSTX1 A3/A2 = 2Y/2Z, 9/8 CAN B10/B11) and U52 (14/13 SSTX2 B2/B3 = 1Y/1Z, 12/11 CAN A11/A10, 9 CC2 B5, 8 AUX_CAB A8/B8) TPD6E05U06RVZ, pin order follows the J50 pad rows (TI SLVSBO7O Table 5.4 p.7: 0.47\n  pF, VRWM 5.5 V); place within a few mm of J50. D+/D- clamp is U61 on the Controller sheet.\nCAN: no termination on the module (SLLA270 p.4, p.8); R182/R183/C180 are DNP for a single-module bench; never fit them on a module in a star. 125\n  kbit/s PROPOSED. Two bused pairs give about 45 ohm in parallel, acceptable at the slowed edges.\nShield: S1 to GND through C181 1 nF with R170 1 M (DNP). Layout rules (not schematic): Dp/Dn ties within 3.5 mm of J50 (TC Table 3-4 note 1 p.77).\nUNRESOLVED: top- or mid-mount J50; SBU exposure to a laptop alternate mode; unidirectional ESD clamp near -0.7 V versus cable GND drop on CAN; the 3.3\n  V-only ESP32 GPIO behind R186 1k."
		(exclude_from_sim yes)
		(at 38.1 232 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.1 1.1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "3b357cd1-4021-40f7-94f4-673b973014cf")
	)
	(text "J50 pin map (WE 632723300011 p.3, TC Table 3-4 p.76; A5/B5 are labelled CC/VCONN by Wuerth, wired as CC1/CC2: PROPOSED reading)\nA1 GND  A2 SSTXP1=LVDS_OUT1_P  A3 SSTXN1=LVDS_OUT1_N  A4 VBUS  A5 CC1  A6 DP1=USB_DP  A7 DN1=USB_DM  A8 SBU1=AUX_CAB  A9 VBUS  A10 SSRXN2=CAN_L  A11\n  SSRXP2=CAN_H  A12 GND\nB1 GND  B2 SSTXP2=LVDS_OUT2_P  B3 SSTXN2=LVDS_OUT2_N  B4 VBUS  B5 CC2  B6 DP2=USB_DP  B7 DN2=USB_DM  B8 SBU2=AUX_CAB  B9 VBUS  B10 SSRXN1=CAN_L  B11\n  SSRXP1=CAN_H  B12 GND\nJ51 DEBUG (2.54 mm 1x6): 1 GND, 2 LVDS_DBG_P (U50 3Y), 3 LVDS_DBG_N (U50 3Z), 4 CAN_H, 5 CAN_L, 6 AUX.\nTest points TP50-TP55: 3V3, 3V3_D, RSSI, HV_MON, GND, GND. DNP: R170, R177, R182, R183, C180.\nCable rule: passive full-featured USB 3.2 Gen 1, 3 A, e-marked, <= 2 m certified; 3 m only after a bench check (TC Table 3-1 p.44, 3.4.1.1 p.83, 4.4.1\n  p.151). Labelling: USB-C: USB 2.0 and 5 V only on a host; SuperSpeed pairs carry proprietary LVDS/CAN, not USB 3; the module is not USB 3 compliant.\nHV rule: no bare APD_BIAS pad on this sheet; HV_MON (about Vout/101) is the only HV observation point.\nULX3S target pairs (PROPOSED; ULX3S schematics v3.1.7 p.2, Lattice FPGA-TN-02032 v1.4 p.14, p.26): first choice gp/gn[8..13] (bank 7), second\n  gp/gn[14..21]; not [0..7] or [22..27]. Constrain gp only; do not guess polarity."
		(exclude_from_sim yes)
		(at 200 232 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.1 1.1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "17250198-36bf-444a-a95d-78adf9bd2a2e")
	)
